      "text": "Powder processing builds dense solid parts from powder feedstock. It is the dominant manufacturing route for cemented carbide cutting tools, PM steels, and advanced ceramics — materials that cannot be economically cast or machined to final shape. The key physics: sintering drives densification by reducing surface energy."
